# UFW and Sysctl configuration conflict #

Even if the rules were added on the 

PATH:/etc/sysctl.conf

the system might follow the 

PATH:/etc/ufw/sysctl.conf

To make the rules are being followed from 

PATH:/etc/sysctl.conf

change path variable of the 

# Key pairs #

{

IPT_SYSCTL=/etc/ufw/sysctl.conf to 

IPT_SYSCTL=/etc/sysctl.conf

}

on the file 

Path:/etc/default/ufw

Once done need to restart the UFW 

<sudo ufw disable>

<sudo ufw enable>



# To disable ipv6 disable set 1 below or to enable set 0

Path:/etc/sysctl

<nano /etc/sysctl.conf>

# Key pairs #

{

net.ipv6.conf.all.disable_ipv6 = 1
net.ipv6.conf.default.disable_ipv6 = 1
net.ipv6.conf.lo.disable_ipv6 = 1

}

# To apply the changes #

<sudo sysctl -p>

<sysctl --system>



# Verify IPv6 is disabled #

<cat /proc/sys/net/ipv6/conf/all/disable_ipv6>

# GRUB Kernel Parameter (Recommended for full disable) #

Edit GRUB config:

<nano /etc/default/grub>

Modify this line:

}

From:

GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX=""

To:

GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX="ipv6.disable=1"
GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX_DEFAULT="quiet splash ipv6.disable=1"

}


incase the GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX already contains an configuration

GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX="apparmor=1 security=apparmor ipv6.disable=1"


Update GRUB:

<sudo update-grub>

Reboot:

<sudo reboot>

Verify:

/bin/grep -Pqs '^\h*0\b' /sys/module/ipv6/parameters/disable && echo -e "\n - IPv6 is enabled\n" || echo -e "\n - IPv6 is not enabled\n"
